 fans out there  who would happily buy Cinderella's ball  gown or Ariel's dinglehopper within two  years of its launch the Disney Princess  brand brought in over three billion in  sells the brand offers products from  children's toys and costumes to high-end  cosmetics and Couture the brands appeals  to everyone equally that's a lot of  princess glam with that kind of selling  power it's easy to see why Disney is so  picky about who received a royal  coronation not every royal character  gets to be part of this wildly popular  franchise the original lineup was Snow  White Cinderella Aurora Ariel Belle  Jasmine Pocahontas Mulan and Tinkerbell  in 2005 the lineup changed Disney  noticed the popularity of their fairy  characters and stories and decided to  launch the official Disney fairy brand  Tinkerbell left her throne as an  official Disney Princess and became the  face of the fairy franchise in 2010  Tiana from The Princess and the Frog  enjoyed an extravagant coronation in  2011 Rapunzel was added as well two  years later the first Pixar character  was added to the list with Meredith fans  have speculated for years just what gets  a character on the list the answer may  surprise you  royal heritage isn't a requirement  neither Pocahontas Mulan or Tinkerbell  have any titles there are several  daughters of kings and queens who  haven't made the list either official  princesses don't even have to be the  star of their film Jasmine wasn't the  main protagonists in Aladdin after all  fans have wondered of being human with  requirements but Ariel was once a  mermaid and the original lineup included  a fairy any character introduced in a  sequel is automatically out of the  running as well many may have thought  Disney revealed the big secret with a  line in one of their movies in Moana  Maui refers to Moana as princess  she proudly corrects the demigod that  she's in fact the daughter of a chief  now even says that many believe to be  the Disney princess secret sauce 